.DS_Store
/target
# Cargo.lock IS tracked. yoyo-agent is a binary crate ([[bin]] name = "yoyo"),
# and Cargo's guidance for binaries is to commit the lock so builds are
# reproducible. It was ignored from the initial commit — the library-crate
# default, never a decision — and the cost was measured on 2026-08-24: yoagent
# 0.16.6 shipped, CI resolved it unasked, and its CORRECTION of the sonnet-5
# preset ($3/$15 -> $2/$10) surfaced as a yoyo test failure with no yoyo change.
# main was red for 31 hours. Release builds had the same hole: two builds of
# identical source could ship different dependency versions to the four
# platform binaries install.sh distributes.
#
# The tradeoff, accepted deliberately: dependency bumps are now explicit
# commits instead of arriving free. For a self-evolving agent that is the
# better default — an upstream change becomes something yoyo can see and
# reason about, rather than an invisible break in a test it never touched.
